comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T12:54:11.011Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status strict-read census covered 2,609 items with no unreadable rows, no omissions, no truncation, and no continuation. Exact GH-1166 and root-help --all searches found only closed predecessor pm-e2bq plus umbrella pm-n7rr; this recurrence needs a new issue rather than reopening completed shipped work. GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1166"
  "2026-08-31T12:54:40.370Z","harness:codex","TDD start: add failing structured and process-level assertions that compact root help advertises --all while retaining the compact command tier and full discovery behavior."
  "2026-08-31T15:13:31.095Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: linked compact-help and process-level discovery suite passed 8 tests. Compact text and JSON root help advertise --all, the compact tier remains bounded, and pm --all retains the complete public catalog. Exact 100% repository coverage, typecheck, contract generation, command grammar, npx/bunx packed smoke, and isolated npm+Bun acceptance passed. GitHub issue #1166 is linked to this canonical item."
  "2026-08-31T16:11:24.301Z","harness:codex","Hosted review evidence: the compatibility Claude plugin smoke now locks the expanded 32-tool catalog and its user-facing docs, closing the hosted smokes failure caused by the newly added pm_discover tool. DeepScan nullable-access findings in progressive tools/list coverage were fixed with explicit runtime shape validation."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T15:07:56.770Z","harness:codex",A compact discovery surface must advertise its own expansion control; an implemented --all flag is effectively hidden when compact help omits it.
